    <string name="st_cursor_render">Pointer rendering</string>
    <string name="st_cursor_render_pc">Computer pointer</string>
    <string name="st_cursor_render_pc_sub">Your computer draws the cursor over the video. Nothing below changes what you see.</string>
    <string name="st_cursor_render_phone">Phone pointer</string>
    <string name="st_cursor_render_phone_sub">Android draws the cursor into the stream. Needed for the styles below — and it holds on to your mouse.</string>
    <string name="st_cursor_render_note">Held means the pointer stays inside the desktop window: a phone-drawn cursor is a relative mouse, and it only moves while the pointer is held. Press Alt (or Super) to hand the mouse back to the computer.</string>
    <string name="st_touchpad">Touchpad gestures</string>
    <string name="st_touchpad_sub">Use three fingers on your laptop\'s touchpad to drive the desktop</string>
    <string name="st_touchpad_none">No touchpad was found on the connected computer, so nothing here does anything yet. A mouse wheel and right-click already work without it.</string>
    <string name="st_touchpad_permission">The desktop app cannot read your trackpad until you allow it: System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Accessibility.</string>
    <string name="st_touchpad_takeover">While the desktop is open, your computer\'s own three-finger gestures are switched off so they do not fire alongside these, and switched back on when it closes. Four-finger gestures are left alone. On Windows, if the computer still switches apps behind the desktop, sign out of Windows once.</string>
